## Nullable message property codec inputs — 2026-10-15

- Added Rust adapters for Java `MessageDecoder.messageProperties2String` with a null map and null key/value entries, and for `string2messageProperties` with null input. Java omits null values, turns a null key into the literal `null`, and returns an empty map for a null string. The invoked fixture covers those inputs plus empty and malformed/duplicate records; Phase 8 mapping and release checklist are updated. Fixture SHA-256: `b4ae563511220dbf008a4ef0bc30d82f2c325005e36eb52b15a5ee87bff59d40`.
